        cwa_flag: true,
        cwa_alumni: false,
        data_center_case: true,
        data_center_notes: "MAJOR FINDING 2026-08-04: active, escalating scandal — not a quiet filing. Developer approached the Township as early as Jan 2024 under euphemisms ('Project Honeycomb,' 'EcoPower Travel Center') for the Oakridge Golf Course site, later identified as CLOVERLEAF — the SAME developer (Cloverleaf Infrastructure) behind the Dundee Township ('Project Ironwood,' id 350) and Frenchtown Charter Township ('Project Cherry Blossom,' id 352) proposals, both Monroe County — a THIRD Michigan township hit by the same company. Township's 2025 Master Plan quietly added an 'I-94 Development District' absent from earlier drafts. On Jan 28, 2026 the Supervisor's office PUBLICLY DENIED any communication with data-center developers — FOIA'd emails from the same month directly contradict this, showing meeting requests, a zoning map turned around in 15 minutes, and a solicited 'Letter of Support.' Board passed a 4-month moratorium Feb 2, 2026; FOIA emails (Feb 4) show developers had already received and commented on draft township ordinance language before the moratorium was even public. May 4, 2026: Board REJECTED its own Planning Commission's recommended 8-month moratorium extension. ~200 residents turned out June 1-2, 2026 demanding an extension; PC voted 4-2 (June 3) to delay sending the Data Center and 'I-94 Development District' draft ordinances to the Board after the outcry — but a first reading of the I-94 ordinance proceeded anyway July 13, 2026. Four of five Township trustees reportedly face RECALL PETITIONS over this. Developer runs a standalone PR site (lenoxdatacenter.com, 'Lenox's Next Chapter') claiming ~$240M/yr tax revenue with explicit US-vs-China AI-competitiveness framing. RESOLVED 2026-08-04 (evening): CWA's drafting role is CONFIRMED — the March 23, 2026 PC minutes (Mo downloaded directly) show planner Shana Lengyel, 'with Carlisle Wortman Associates, the new Planner for Lenox,' presenting and walking the Commission through both draft ordinances (I-94 Development District rezoning + standalone Data Center ordinance, Sec. 719.157). Corrects prior misattribution to Stephen Cassin. Also from that meeting: noise cap referenced at a flat 65 dB at the property line (matches CWA's usual opening-bid pattern seen at Scio); a proposed 1,350 ft residential setback defended as needing to be 'defendable' / not exclusionary zoning; and — the clearest resident-driven win — data centers were moved from Permitted-by-Right to Special Land Use (discretionary review) status at a commissioner's push. See PACT-Vault Documents/CWA-Ordinance-Pattern-Comparison and People/Ben Carlisle. UPDATE 2026-09-10 (sweep): a Sept 3-4, 2026 ClickOnDetroit investigation adds names and a new astroturfing wrinkle to the same underlying Jan 2026 episode — New Haven Village President Brian Meissen's FOIA request surfaced emails showing a property owner told Supervisor Anthony Reeder Jr. in Jan 2026 'we have been approached by a large data center developer that would like to meet with you,' and the developer sent a draft letter of township support Jan 21, 2026 (the township publicly denied endorsing it Jan 28, 2026 — the same denial-vs-FOIA contradiction already on file above). Residents led by Arianna Welsh continue accusing leadership of stonewalling. New: an anonymous pro-development site (LenoxDataCenter.com, already tracked above) and mailers from a group calling itself 'Michigan Deserves Better' are promoting a hypothetical project and using the township's own phone number, raising an astroturfing concern layered on top of the existing PR campaign. Source: ClickOnDetroit, Sept 3, 2026 — https://www.clickondetroit.com/news/investigations/2026/09/03/data-center-concerns-have-lenox-township-residents-demanding-transparency/",
        notes: "CORRECTED 2026-08-04 (evening): CWA planner is Shana Lengyel, confirmed via the March 23, 2026 PC minutes (prior attribution to Stephen Cassin was wrong). Township hall: 63775 Gratiot Ave, Lenox MI 48050. Township's domain migrated lenoxtwp.org -> lenox-mi.gov in 2026. Resident opposition hub: lenoxdatacenterinfo.org. DATA SYNC 2026-09-05: the top-level planner_name/firm fields had never been updated to match this correction (still read 'Stephen Cassin' for a month) -- fixed today during a Cassin cross-municipality research pass. | COORDINATE CORRECTED 2026-09-11 (statewide close-pair audit, see reference_map_coordinate_corrections.md): moved to Wikipedia infobox township centroid.",
        work_history: null,
        sources: ["https://www.lenox-mi.gov/", "https://www.lenoxdatacenterinfo.org/timeline-of-events/", "https://www.lenoxdatacenterinfo.org/upcoming-meetings/", "https://lenoxdatacenter.com/", "https://planetdetroit.org/2026/07/data-center-news-saline-township/", "https://www.newsbreak.com/mlive-513121/4689291687627-lenox-township-comission-delays-data-center-ordinances-after-resident-outcry"]
