        data_center_case: true,
        data_center_notes: "'Project Flex' is a real ~172-acre, 1.8M sq ft data center proposed by Verrus (a Sidewalk Infrastructure Partners subsidiary backed by Alphabet/StepStone/Ontario Teachers'; CEO Nelson Abramson), which already had preliminary Planning Commission approval (Sept 2025) before the Township's 6-month moratorium on NEW data center projects (enacted Mar 2, 2026 \u2014 explicitly does not apply to Project Flex itself, a clean carve-out for the already-pending application). An active recall petition targets all seven Township trustees (officially tied to an unrelated wage-adjustment vote, though clearly entangled with resident anger over the project). UPDATE 2026-09-13 (a year of developments): the moratorium was extended another 6 months 'in early August 2026,' confirmed by name though the exact date/tally is still unpinned \u2014 this substantiates a previously-unverified debrief claim of an Aug 5 extension vote; that debrief's other two claims (an ethics-policy push, a golf-outing conflict callout) remain uncorroborated. End customer reported as Anthropic. Organized opposition group 'No Data Center Lyon Township' (organizers Craig Kreutzberg, Melisa Noble) has filed FOIA requests; the township's own hired reviewers \u2014 K&S Engineers (noise) and Code Concepts Group (fire code) \u2014 flagged compliance gaps in Verrus's own studies. Verrus has proposed a $10M community-benefits package. A new 120kV transmission line, relocated stormwater pond, and reduced lighting have all been added/adjusted since initial approval; the latest Aug 13, 2026 submission adds an 18-ft acoustic wall. The Sept 14, 2026 Planning Commission meeting was expected to be the final site-plan decision one year after conditional approval, but the Township pulled Project Flex from that agenda after a retrospective piece ran \u2014 status unresolved as of this writing; both sides have signaled possible litigation. FURTHER UPDATED 2026-09-13 (60-day news sweep, re-run directly after the first pass hit a search-budget limit): a fourth application was submitted mid-July 2026 (Aug 24, 2026 PC review anticipated), then a fifth revision Aug 13, 2026. Per a Sept 8, 2026 Livingston Post retrospective (Part II), no litigation has been filed by either side and Verrus now says it favors negotiating with the township over suing. Distinct from the unrelated Lyon Township near Higgins Lake, Roscommon County. Sources: Detroit News (moratorium) \u2014 https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/local/oakland-county/2026/03/03/as-project-flex-proceeds-lyon-township-hits-pause-on-new-data-centers/88960710007/ ; Detroit News (recall) \u2014 https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/local/oakland-county/2026/05/06/group-looks-to-recall-lyon-trustees-over-data-center-with-unrelated-language/89929672007/ ; The Livingston Post, 'Project Flex, One Year Later, Part I & II,' Sept 8 2026 \u2014 https://thelivingstonpost.com/project-flex-one-year-later-part-i/ , https://thelivingstonpost.com/project-flex-one-year-later-part-ii/ UPDATE 2026-09-20 (weekly sweep): the moratorium extension reported in early August 2026 was described as running \"through September 8, 2026\" per the March 2026 board synopsis language — that date has now passed (12+ days as of Sept 20) with no public source found confirming a further extension, a lapse, or a permanent ordinance. Needs a direct check of Lyon's post-Sept 8 board minutes: https://lyontwp-higginsmi.gov/minutes-and-reports/ and https://www.lyontwp.org/government/township_boards_and_commissions/planning_commission_.php CORRECTED 2026-09-20 (later same-day pass): the moratorium was in fact re-extended 6 more months in early August 2026 — it did NOT lapse on Sept 8 as the note above speculated. Also new: Verrus submitted a 5th site-plan revision Aug 13, 2026; it was floated for the Sept 14 Planning Commission agenda but the township confirmed it would not be on that agenda — next hearing date TBD.",
        notes: "lyontwp.org blocks automated access via robots.txt. Distinct from Lyon Township, Wayne County if one exists on other trackers -- this is Lyon Township, OAKLAND County (Milford/South Lyon area). Anthropic as an end-user is a first for this map -- watch for more Anthropic-linked Michigan sites. | MERGED 2026-09-11: consolidated from a duplicate record (formerly id 1654) found in the statewide duplicate-record audit. | CONFIRMED 2026-09-13 (Oakland County completeness research): McKenna Associates serves as the Township's planning consultant; Patrick Sloan and Brian Keesey are the assigned planners. Note: the Township's retained legal counsel, Rosati Schultz Joppich & Amtsbuechler PC, is the same firm representing the City of Wixom against Wixom Industrial One, LLC in the federal data-center lawsuit tracked elsewhere on this map \u2014 a cross-reference worth watching, not evidence of any impropriety here.",
