        data_center_notes: "UPDATED 2026-08-04: NOT a CWA site — confirmed planner is Lucie Fortin of The Mannik & Smith Group (also Bedford Township's planner); legal counsel is Fahey, Schultz, Burzych and Rhodes. Active proposal: Cloverleaf Infrastructure ('Project Ironwood,' ironwooddatacenter.com), ~750 acres under option spanning Dundee Twp/Milan Twp, ~350-acre footprint at Ann Arbor Rd & Day Rd, $1B+ (up to $8-10B fully built) — developer withdrew its pre-development agreement Sept 30/Oct 8 2025 citing insufficient community engagement; Village of Dundee separately voted to block water supply. Moratorium adopted Oct 14 2025, extended Dec 9 2025 (Res. 5-2025) to 180 days, extended AGAIN via Resolution 2026-4 (adopted at the May 12 2026 meeting) to run June 22, 2026–June 22, 2027 — currently active. Draft ordinance concepts per Dec 9 2025 minutes (12-ft berm/3-layer evergreen screening, 30-ft max height, 750-ft setback from Dundee Blvd, 50 dBA noise limit, decommissioning bonds, monitoring wells) do NOT match the CWA template (no 'benefits are balanced with' language, no 75% materials standard, no PUE cap, no renewable-sourcing %) — a useful CONTRAST case (independently drafted via Mannik & Smith, not CWA), though the full ordinance isn't finalized yet (public workshop scheduled Aug 12, 2026). Cloverleaf is separately pursuing a companion site in neighboring Frenchtown Charter Township (id 352, also non-CWA). Distinct from the Village of Dundee (id 359) — a separate government whose own strategic-plan SWOT flags 'Data Center' as a top resident concern, almost certainly reacting to this same project. See PACT-Vault Documents/CWA-Ordinance-Pattern-Comparison and People/Ben Carlisle. | COORDINATE CORRECTED 2026-09-11 (statewide duplicate-coordinate cluster audit, see reference_map_coordinate_corrections.md): moved from shared county-centroid placeholder (41.96, -83.661) to individually-verified Wikipedia infobox coordinate.",
