        data_center_notes: "ACTIVE/ONGOING as of Aug 19, 2026. A former marijuana-growing facility (\"Harbor Farmz\", CEO Michael Ward) at 2839 Full Circle Drive, Davis Creek Business Park, Milwood neighborhood, contacted CPED in March 2026 about converting to a data center; city staff determined this would be a permitted use under the existing M-2 (heavy industrial) zoning, no rezoning required. Reported scale: current facility 32,850 sq ft, current draw ~1 MW, potential capacity up to 15 MW, with a 600 kW backup generator. No formal site plan application filed as of the article dates (June-July 2026). NEW (2026-08-17/19): City Commission unanimously adopted a 1-year moratorium the night of Aug 17, 2026, covering data centers, battery energy storage systems (BESS), crypto mining, and AI facilities citywide — resolving the informal discussion first raised by Vice Mayor Drew Duncan in July. CivicClerk agenda portal is JS-rendered and inaccessible to automated fetch — sources below are news coverage, not primary municipal record. UPDATE 2026-09-10 (30-day sweep): Planning Commission unanimously approved (up to 1-year) moratorium language covering data centers, crypto mining, AND battery storage facilities on Sept 9, 2026 -- appears to be the Planning Commission\u0027s formal follow-through on the Aug 17 City Commission action noted above, not a separate incident (exact procedural relationship between the two votes not fully clear from coverage -- worth a direct confirm). Source: WKZO, Sept 9, 2026.",
