        data_center_notes: "NEW (2026-08-19, cross-referenced from MLive's statewide data center tracking map): unnamed tech company exploring Solon Township for a potential data center dubbed 'Project Peninsula.' Status: Proposed — township officials are developing data center rules and passed a temporary moratorium; anonymous developers have indicated interest but no formal plans have been submitted. Source: MLive, Jun 2026 — https://www.mlive.com/news/grand-rapids/2026/06/west-michigan-town-tables-data-center-vote-after-residents-demand-stricter-rules.html MAJOR UPDATE 2026-08-21 (30-day sweep): the applicant is now understood to operate through a shell company, VENERLY LLC; Consumers Energy has separately confirmed a 1GW data-center load commitment in its service territory believed tied to this project, though no commercial end-user/operator has been publicly named. Planning Commission tabled an 800-acre-cap Special Land Use ordinance Jul 22, 2026 after community pushback; retained special counsel Michael Homier Jul 27, 2026 to lead ordinance redrafting; a related 17 Mile Rd rezoning was also tabled pending the ordinance work. Opposition group \"Stop Solon Township Data Center\" submitted comments on ordinance draft #5 on Aug 9, 2026. MAJOR UPDATE 2026-09-10 (sweep): Aug 25, 2026 — Board voted 3-2 to hire McKenna Associates for Master Plan/Future Land Use map updates (criticized for only ~26 hours' public notice). Aug 26, 2026 — Planning Commission unanimously voted to move the six-month moratorium-extension ordinance to the Board of Trustees (moratorium now extended a further 6 months beyond the original Feb 2026 term), tabled the 17 Mile Road rezoning pending McKenna's review, and formally introduced special counsel Michael Homier (Foster Swift) to the Commission. Sept 2, 2026 — staff meeting introduced Homier and the McKenna planning team to discuss the master-plan timeline. Sources: WOODTV; Data Center Dynamics; Stop Solon Township Data Center timeline (stopsolontownshipdatacenter.com); Michigan Advance Weekly Download, Aug 31 2026.",
